# Pinned working trees — one `<absolute-path> <branch>` per line.
#
# A path listed here may not leave <branch>: the reference-transaction hook
# aborts any HEAD update that would switch it away or detach it. Unlisted paths
# are untouched, so `git init`, `git clone` and `git worktree add` keep working
# everywhere else. The line is whitespace-split, so a path containing a space is
# not supported; `~/` expands to $HOME (a literal `$HOME` does not), and a
# trailing slash is ignored. Record the path in its PHYSICAL form — what
# `pwd -P` prints inside the tree. The hook resolves symlinks on its own side
# but not on this one, so a path reached through a symlinked directory would
# never match.
#
# Override for one command:  DOTFILES_ALLOW_UNPIN=1 <git command>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy worktrees. Each is a linked worktree whose branch decides what a
# `make buca` from it ships, so a switch here deploys the wrong code.
#
# Absolute, not `~/`: a `~/` entry is expanded against the HOME of whoever runs
# git, so it silently stops matching for a launchd/systemd daemon (no HOME) or a
# process running as another user. The hook refuses rather than allows when it
# meets a `~/` entry it cannot expand, but absolute paths avoid the question.
